SWEET CHG P1 (patch 0283, charger bring-up phase 1, docs/research/charger-max77759-gs101.md section 8 steps 1-2): READ-ONLY witness of the state ABL left around the MAX77759 I2C bus (HSI2C12 / USI12 on PERIC1) so the later bring-up (a separate review-gated patch) starts from measured values, not guesses. Default ON, opt-out boot-arg sweetchgprobe=0. NO hardware store anywhere in this patch: every window is mapped `const volatile` and one allowlist-checked function does all loads (bsd/dev/sweet_chg.c). Once, from the USB-log drain thread after the log socket exists, it prints `SWEET CHG P1:` lines: stage A reads the six CMU_PERIC1 words, three CMU_TOP words, sysreg_peric1 SW_CONF, gpp23 CON/DAT/PUD and logs the implied IPCLK; the gate decision chg_gate_open() (IPCLK/PCLK/RSTNSYNC gates CG_VAL=1 auto=0, QCH CLOCK_REQ=1, mux not busy, top IP gate open if selected) then permits or forbids stage B, one log round later, which reads the HSI2C12 USI_CON/CTL/CONF/FIFO_STATUS/TIMING_FS1-3/TRANS_STATUS/INT_STATUS. A gated clock logs `SWEET CHG GAP: hsi2c12 clock gated, block not read (...)` and the 0x10D50000 window is never accessed (AP-113). New ADT node /sweet-chg from tools/mkadt.py add_chg_node <- soc/google/gs101/soc.json chg_probe. Hooked by one call in ud_log_thread (bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c). Applies after 0279. Host test: tools/test_chg_probe.py. Read-only; the first run is the review of what ABL leaves.

